1. The Protagonist’s Rebirth: Becoming a PodCast Host
The protagonist has endured a long period of despair.
His life and spirit had both sunk into darkness.

One day, in a quiet room, he starts a small radio program
and begins to speak calmly about his own life.
It is not meant for anyone in particular.
It is simply “an act of leaving behind a record of having lived.”

■ The “Deep Sea” He Reveals on Air
His family was turned into a meme and mocked online
He lost all his savings and his life collapsed
His mental state collapsed, and he was labeled as mentally ill
His former wife was taken by his superior
In the whistleblowing trial, the company was declared innocent
He was the only one confined to a locked ward
He kept going because there was nothing else he could do.
A close friend eventually helped him stand back up
And now, he no longer holds hatred toward anyone

He knew it well.
There are countless radio shows in the world.
No one would listen to his voice.

Still, he spoke.
Quietly, plainly, only the facts.

He never expected the program to make money.

■ Encounter with the Mentor
One day, a seasoned PodCast host—
moved by the honesty of his storytelling—reaches out to him.

“Why don’t you create a show of your own?”

In that moment, the protagonist realizes for the first time
that his voice is being recognized as “work.”

The show gradually gains popularity,
leading to a flow of
monetization → financial recovery → emotional recovery.

Seeking something that symbolizes his new self,
he decides to travel to Milan.

